I ascended for the second time today, with a female tourist named Yoda.
Which just goes to show, if you pick a name you like, you're doomed to
be killed by blue ants, but if you choose a stupid throw-away name,
you're bound to ascend!

Yoda was very conservative, avoiding all fights as long as possible,
and she knew things were going her way when she found a shield of
reflection in a shop around level 2.  When she got down to minetown,
things turned scary.  There were not one or two, but five or six dead
adventurers haunting the place... they had about 3 wands of polymorph
but not a bag of holding between them.  Yoda's beastly mutt was quickly
killed when it tried to eat the entire town guard at once, as well as a
rock troll that was there.  A lucky scroll of taming allowed her to
recruit the troll as a pet (named Chesleigh) who stayed with her all
the way through to the Plane of Air... unfortunately she was in a bit
of a rush to get to the portal and didn't want to take the couple of
turns it would take to summon him then jump through!

There was also a yellow dragon running around minetown, and no priest
left alive, but this is a story already told.

>From there it was pretty straightforward; reflection at an early level
is wonderful.  She got jumping boots and used them to take on medusa,
then used the drawbridge trick to empty the castle (first time i did
that).  She didn't even need to use all the wand's charges as she had
gotten grayswandir from an early magic lamp, and was otherwise
well-outfitted.

About the time she entered Rodney's zoo she realized it was a poor
string of luck that she hadn't gotten conflict yet.  Fishing for her
wand of wishing in the bag, she couldn't find it, and realized she must
have polypiled it back a while.  So, she confused tamed all the
beasties.  Same trick worked well in Moloch's sanctum.  Ultimately she
knew she wanted conflict, though, so she polypiled for it on the way
back up, using an old stash of rings.

The planes were easy with a crystal ball, lev boots, and conflict ring.
 She'd just sit inside a steam vortex or whatever and apply the crystal
ball.  Air was quite scary as a Titan kept summoning beasties, cutting
off her path, and air elementals were still targeting her despite the
conflict ring.  She got caught inside one while in the crystal ball
trance, and went from 250hp down to maybe 60.


